// Writing to a child's input after it closed it fails with broken_pipe. On Linux and
// macOS the write also raises SIGPIPE, which this program ignores itself: std leaves
// that to the program.
// The child is tests/helpers/child.ctx, as `close_input`: it closes its standard input, prints
// `closed`, and sleeps for a minute.
//# build child: {home}/tests/helpers/child.ctx
//# build program: main.ctx
//# $ {program} {child}
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| broken pipe
//| 137
